Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: bcm fullcone: do not unregister the BCM-NAT helper

The BCM-NAT helper is assigned to conntracks directly and is never
passed to nf_conntrack_helper_register(), so its list node is not
hashed. Unregistering it dereferences a NULL pprev, which crashes the
kernel when nft_masq or xt_MASQUERADE is unloaded.

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_nat_masquerade.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_nat_masquerade.c
@@ -560,7 +560,6 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(nf_nat_masquerade_inet
 
 void nf_nat_masquerade_inet_unregister_notifiers(void)
 {
-       nf_conntrack_helper_unregister(&nf_conntrack_helper_bcm_nat);
 	mutex_lock(&masq_mutex);
 	/* check if the notifiers still have clients */
 	if (--masq_refcnt > 0)
